<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35554" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perspergo</span></b> , ĕre, v.
			a.
		per-spargo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to besprinkle</i>, <i>to wet.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ligna amureā crudā
					perspergito,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 130</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unde haustā aquā templum
					deae perspersum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 15, 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prusiadem urbem perspergit Hylas lacus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 42, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orationem tamquam sale,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 1, 34, 159</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
